    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/QCOM.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/QCOM.png",
    "website": "https://www.qualcomm.com",
    "ceo": "Cristiano Renno Amon",
    "full_time_employees": "52000",
    "description": "QUALCOMM Incorporated is a company dedicated to developing and bringing to market fundamental technologies crucial for the global wireless communication industry. Its operations are structured into three primary segments: Qualcomm CDMA Technologies (QCT), Qualcomm Technology Licensing (QTL), and Qualcomm Strategic Initiatives (QSI). The QCT division specializes in creating and supplying integrated circuits and system software, leveraging 3G, 4G, 5G, and other advanced wireless technologies. These components are essential for a range of products, including those used for wireless voice and data communication, networking, application processing, multimedia, and global positioning. The QTL segment generates revenue by licensing its extensive intellectual property portfolio, which encompasses various patent rights vital for the manufacture and sale of wireless devices, particularly those adhering to standards like CDMA2000, WCDMA, LTE, and OFDMA-based 5G. Through its QSI segment, Qualcomm invests in early-stage companies across diverse sectors such as 5G, artificial intelligence, automotive, consumer electronics, enterprise solutions, cloud computing, and the Internet of Things, aiming to support the introduction of new products and services for both existing and emerging communication applications. Furthermore, the company provides development services and related products to United States government agencies and their contractors. Founded in 1985, QUALCOMM Incorporated maintains its headquarters in San Diego, California.",
    "description_en": "QUALCOMM Incorporated is a company dedicated to developing and bringing to market fundamental technologies crucial for the global wireless communication industry. Its operations are structured into three primary segments: Qualcomm CDMA Technologies (QCT), Qualcomm Technology Licensing (QTL), and Qualcomm Strategic Initiatives (QSI). The QCT division specializes in creating and supplying integrated circuits and system software, leveraging 3G, 4G, 5G, and other advanced wireless technologies. These components are essential for a range of products, including those used for wireless voice and data communication, networking, application processing, multimedia, and global positioning. The QTL segment generates revenue by licensing its extensive intellectual property portfolio, which encompasses various patent rights vital for the manufacture and sale of wireless devices, particularly those adhering to standards like CDMA2000, WCDMA, LTE, and OFDMA-based 5G. Through its QSI segment, Qualcomm invests in early-stage companies across diverse sectors such as 5G, artificial intelligence, automotive, consumer electronics, enterprise solutions, cloud computing, and the Internet of Things, aiming to support the introduction of new products and services for both existing and emerging communication applications. Furthermore, the company provides development services and related products to United States government agencies and their contractors. Founded in 1985, QUALCOMM Incorporated maintains its headquarters in San Diego, California.",
    "description_zh": "高通公司 (QCOM) 係全球無線通訊產業之基礎技術先驅，致力於開發並推動關鍵技術上市。其營運架構主要分為三大事業體：高通CDMA技術部門 (QCT)、高通技術授權部門 (QTL) 及高通策略投資部門 (QSI)。\n\nQCT部門專責設計與供應整合型晶片及系統軟體，運用3G、4G、5G等先進無線通訊技術。這些組件廣泛應用於無線語音與數據通訊、網路連線、應用處理、多媒體及全球定位等產品。\n\nQTL部門透過授權其涵蓋CDMA2000、WCDMA、LTE及OFDMA 5G等關鍵標準之廣泛智慧財產權組合，提供無線設備製造與銷售所需之專利技術，藉此獲取營收。\n\nQSI部門則投資5G、人工智慧、車用電子、消費性電子、企業解決方案、雲端運算及物聯網等新興領域之早期新創公司，旨在推動現有與未來通訊應用之新產品與服務上市。\n\n此外，高通亦向美國政府機構及其承包商提供開發服務與相關產品。高通公司成立於1985年，總部位於加州聖地牙哥。",
