    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/LRCX.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/LRCX.png",
    "website": "https://www.lamresearch.com",
    "ceo": "Timothy Archer",
    "full_time_employees": "23300",
    "description": "Lam Research Corporation is a prominent supplier of equipment vital for semiconductor processing, encompassing its design, production, sales, repair, and ongoing maintenance. These sophisticated systems are fundamental for the creation of integrated circuits. The company's extensive product catalog features a variety of deposition technologies. For tungsten metallization, they provide ALTUS systems that deposit conformal films. SABRE products excel in electrochemical deposition, crucial for copper interconnect transitions and enabling copper damascene manufacturing. SOLA utilizes ultraviolet thermal processing for film treatments, while VECTOR delivers plasma-enhanced chemical vapor deposition (CVD) and atomic layer deposition (ALD) solutions. Furthermore, SPEED addresses gapfill applications with its high-density plasma CVD products, and Striker is engineered for single-wafer atomic layer deposition of dielectric films. Beyond deposition, Lam Research offers a comprehensive suite of etching tools. Flex is designed for dielectric etch applications, Kiyo handles conductor etch processes, Syndion specializes in through-silicon via etching, and Versys metal products are used for metal etch processes. The company's offerings also extend to specialized solutions like Coronus, which enhances die yield through bevel cleaning. For various wafer cleaning requirements, Lam Research supplies multiple product lines, including Da Vinci, DV-Prime, EOS, and SP series. Additionally, Metryx mass metrology systems provide precise, in-line mass measurement capabilities for semiconductor wafer manufacturing. Lam Research serves the global semiconductor industry, distributing its technologies and services across the United States, China, Europe, Japan, Korea, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, and other international markets. Established in 1980, the company maintains its corporate headquarters in Fremont, California.",
    "description_en": "Lam Research Corporation is a prominent supplier of equipment vital for semiconductor processing, encompassing its design, production, sales, repair, and ongoing maintenance. These sophisticated systems are fundamental for the creation of integrated circuits. The company's extensive product catalog features a variety of deposition technologies. For tungsten metallization, they provide ALTUS systems that deposit conformal films. SABRE products excel in electrochemical deposition, crucial for copper interconnect transitions and enabling copper damascene manufacturing. SOLA utilizes ultraviolet thermal processing for film treatments, while VECTOR delivers plasma-enhanced chemical vapor deposition (CVD) and atomic layer deposition (ALD) solutions. Furthermore, SPEED addresses gapfill applications with its high-density plasma CVD products, and Striker is engineered for single-wafer atomic layer deposition of dielectric films. Beyond deposition, Lam Research offers a comprehensive suite of etching tools. Flex is designed for dielectric etch applications, Kiyo handles conductor etch processes, Syndion specializes in through-silicon via etching, and Versys metal products are used for metal etch processes. The company's offerings also extend to specialized solutions like Coronus, which enhances die yield through bevel cleaning. For various wafer cleaning requirements, Lam Research supplies multiple product lines, including Da Vinci, DV-Prime, EOS, and SP series. Additionally, Metryx mass metrology systems provide precise, in-line mass measurement capabilities for semiconductor wafer manufacturing. Lam Research serves the global semiconductor industry, distributing its technologies and services across the United States, China, Europe, Japan, Korea, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, and other international markets. Established in 1980, the company maintains its corporate headquarters in Fremont, California.",
    "description_zh": "科林研發（Lam Research, LRCX）為全球領先的半導體製造設備供應商，提供從設計、製造、銷售到維修與支援的完整服務鏈，其精密系統為積體電路製造不可或缺的關鍵。\n\n公司核心業務聚焦於薄膜沉積與蝕刻兩大領域。沉積技術涵蓋鎢金屬化（ALTUS）、電化學沉積（SABRE，用於銅導線互連與鑲嵌製程）、紫外光熱處理（SOLA）、電漿輔助化學氣相沉積（PECVD）與原子層沉積（ALD）設備（如VECTOR、Striker），以及高密度電漿化學氣相沉積（HDPCVD）的縫隙填充方案（SPEED）。蝕刻設備則包括介電蝕刻（Flex）、導體蝕刻（Kiyo）、矽穿孔（TSV）蝕刻（Syndion）及金屬蝕刻（Versys）等多元應用。\n\n此外，科林研發亦提供提升晶粒良率的晶圓邊緣清洗（Coronus）、多系列晶圓清洗設備（如Da Vinci、SP系列），以及用於半導體晶圓製造中精確線上質量量測的Metryx系統。\n\n其技術與服務廣泛應用於全球半導體產業，主要市場涵蓋美國、中國、歐洲、日本、韓國、東南亞與台灣等地。公司成立於1980年，總部設於美國加州弗里蒙特。",
