    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TYL.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TYL.png",
    "website": "https://www.tylertech.com",
    "ceo": "H. Lynn Moore Jr.",
    "full_time_employees": "7879",
    "description": "Tyler Technologies, Inc. specializes in delivering comprehensive information management solutions and services tailored for the public sector. Its operations are organized into three primary divisions: Enterprise Software, Appraisal and Tax, and NIC. The company's extensive product portfolio encompasses financial management tools, such as modular fund accounting systems designed for government bodies and non-profit organizations, as well as utility billing platforms for managing both metered and unmetered services. Additionally, Tyler offers solutions that automate a wide array of municipal and county operations, ranging from municipal court and parking ticket administration to animal and business licensing, permits and inspections, code enforcement, citizen complaint resolution, ambulance billing, fleet maintenance, and cemetery records management. Educational institutions, particularly K-12 schools, benefit from their specialized student information and transportation management systems. Furthermore, the company delivers a comprehensive suite of judicial technologies, including systems for court case management, integrated court and law enforcement functions, prosecutor support, and supervision. These solutions are scalable for diverse needs, from single-county deployments to multi-jurisdictional or statewide implementations. Their offerings extend to public safety software, alongside systems designed for the automated appraisal and assessment of both real and personal property, complemented by tax billing and collection applications for relevant agencies. Public sector agencies also leverage Tyler's software for planning, regulatory compliance, and maintenance operations. Dedicated applications enhance and automate records and document management, while their data and insights solutions provide valuable analytical capabilities. Beyond core software, Tyler Technologies facilitates Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) deployments and provides electronic document filing solutions for legal and judicial entities. Their service portfolio is robust, encompassing software and hardware installation, data conversion, user training, product customization, and ongoing maintenance and support. They also offer outsourced property appraisal services to taxing authorities. A strategic collaboration agreement with Amazon Web Services (AWS) underscores the company's commitment to cloud-based hosting solutions. Established in 1966, Tyler Technologies, Inc. maintains its headquarters in Plano, Texas.",
    "description_en": "Tyler Technologies, Inc. specializes in delivering comprehensive information management solutions and services tailored for the public sector. Its operations are organized into three primary divisions: Enterprise Software, Appraisal and Tax, and NIC. The company's extensive product portfolio encompasses financial management tools, such as modular fund accounting systems designed for government bodies and non-profit organizations, as well as utility billing platforms for managing both metered and unmetered services. Additionally, Tyler offers solutions that automate a wide array of municipal and county operations, ranging from municipal court and parking ticket administration to animal and business licensing, permits and inspections, code enforcement, citizen complaint resolution, ambulance billing, fleet maintenance, and cemetery records management. Educational institutions, particularly K-12 schools, benefit from their specialized student information and transportation management systems. Furthermore, the company delivers a comprehensive suite of judicial technologies, including systems for court case management, integrated court and law enforcement functions, prosecutor support, and supervision. These solutions are scalable for diverse needs, from single-county deployments to multi-jurisdictional or statewide implementations. Their offerings extend to public safety software, alongside systems designed for the automated appraisal and assessment of both real and personal property, complemented by tax billing and collection applications for relevant agencies. Public sector agencies also leverage Tyler's software for planning, regulatory compliance, and maintenance operations. Dedicated applications enhance and automate records and document management, while their data and insights solutions provide valuable analytical capabilities. Beyond core software, Tyler Technologies facilitates Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) deployments and provides electronic document filing solutions for legal and judicial entities. Their service portfolio is robust, encompassing software and hardware installation, data conversion, user training, product customization, and ongoing maintenance and support. They also offer outsourced property appraisal services to taxing authorities. A strategic collaboration agreement with Amazon Web Services (AWS) underscores the company's commitment to cloud-based hosting solutions. Established in 1966, Tyler Technologies, Inc. maintains its headquarters in Plano, Texas.",
    "description_zh": "Tyler Technologies (TYL) 專為公部門提供全方位資訊管理解決方案與服務，業務聚焦於「企業軟體」、「估價與稅務」及「NIC」三大事業部。核心產品包含模組化基金會計、財務管理、公用事業帳務系統，服務政府機關與非營利組織。其方案廣泛支援市政與郡級營運自動化，涵蓋法院管理、執照核發、稽查、法規執行、市民服務及車隊維護等。\n\n公司亦提供教育機構學生資訊與交通管理系統，並深化司法科技，提供案件管理、執法整合、檢察官支援及監督功能，支援跨轄區部署。產品組合涵蓋公共安全軟體、不動產與動產自動估價評估、稅收管理應用，以及公部門規劃、法規遵循與維護工具，輔以數據分析及文件管理方案。\n\n營運模式包含軟體即服務 (SaaS) 部署，並提供法律與司法電子文件歸檔服務。服務多元，含軟硬體安裝、資料轉移、培訓、客製化與維護；更為稅務機關提供物業估價外包。與Amazon Web Services (AWS) 的策略合作，彰顯雲端託管解決方案實力。",
