    "website": "https://www.arista.com",
    "ceo": "Jayshree V. Ullal",
    "full_time_employees": "5115",
    "description": "Arista Networks, Inc. is a leading global technology firm that designs, promotes, and distributes innovative cloud networking solutions across the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia-Pacific regions. Its comprehensive product portfolio features advanced extensible operating systems, a collection of powerful network applications, and high-performance gigabit Ethernet switching and routing hardware. The company also offers robust post-contract customer support, which includes technical assistance, hardware repairs, parts replacement beyond standard warranty, and critical bug fixes, patches, and upgrades. Arista serves a diverse clientele, encompassing major internet companies, telecommunication providers, financial services organizations, government agencies, and entities in the media and entertainment sectors. Its sales strategy involves multiple channels, utilizing distributors, system integrators, value-added resellers, original equipment manufacturer partners, and a dedicated direct sales force. Established in 2004 as Arastra, Inc., the company adopted the name Arista Networks, Inc. in October 2008 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.",
    "description_en": "Arista Networks, Inc. is a leading global technology firm that designs, promotes, and distributes innovative cloud networking solutions across the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia-Pacific regions. Its comprehensive product portfolio features advanced extensible operating systems, a collection of powerful network applications, and high-performance gigabit Ethernet switching and routing hardware. The company also offers robust post-contract customer support, which includes technical assistance, hardware repairs, parts replacement beyond standard warranty, and critical bug fixes, patches, and upgrades. Arista serves a diverse clientele, encompassing major internet companies, telecommunication providers, financial services organizations, government agencies, and entities in the media and entertainment sectors. Its sales strategy involves multiple channels, utilizing distributors, system integrators, value-added resellers, original equipment manufacturer partners, and a dedicated direct sales force. Established in 2004 as Arastra, Inc., the company adopted the name Arista Networks, Inc. in October 2008 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.",
    "description_zh": "Arista Networks, Inc. (ANET) 為全球領先之雲端網路解決方案供應商，業務遍及美洲、歐洲、中東、非洲與亞太地區。其核心業務聚焦於研發、推廣與銷售創新網路解決方案，旨在協助客戶建構高效、可擴展的網路基礎設施。\n\nANET產品組合涵蓋先進的延伸型作業系統 (Extensible Operating System, EOS)、強大的網路應用程式，以及高效能的Gigabit乙太網路交換器與路由設備。這些產品為資料中心、大型企業園區網路及公有/私有雲環境提供高密度、低延遲的連接能力與軟體定義網路功能。\n\n同時，公司亦提供全面的售後客戶支援服務，包含技術協助、硬體維修、超出標準保固範圍之零件更換，以及關鍵錯誤修復、更新與升級等。其主要服務客群廣泛，涵蓋大型網路服務供應商、電信業者、金融服務機構、政府機關，以及媒體娛樂產業等。\n\nANET的營運模式採用多元通路策略，透過經銷商、系統整合商 (SI)、加值經銷商 (VARs) 及原始設備製造商 (OEM) 夥伴，輔以專業直銷團隊，確保其產品與服務能有效觸及全球市場。",
