    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/APH.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/APH.png",
    "website": "https://www.amphenol.com",
    "ceo": "Richard Adam Norwitt",
    "full_time_employees": "170000",
    "description": "Amphenol Corporation, alongside its numerous subsidiaries, operates globally as a prominent designer, manufacturer, and distributor of electrical, electronic, and fiber optic connectors. Its market reach extends across the United States, China, and various international territories. The company is organized into three primary operational divisions: Harsh Environment Solutions, Communications Solutions, and Interconnect and Sensor Systems. Amphenol's comprehensive product lineup features an extensive array of connectors and integrated connector systems. These include specialized interconnects engineered for demanding conditions (covering data, power, high-speed, fiber optic, and radio frequency applications), in addition to busbars and complete power distribution systems. Beyond these core offerings, the company provides value-added products such as backplane interconnect systems, bespoke cable assemblies and harnesses, and cable management solutions. Their portfolio also encompasses flexible and rigid printed circuit boards (PCBs), hinges, and various other mechanical and production-related components. Furthermore, Amphenol supplies antennas for consumer electronics, network infrastructure, and other uses; a range of coaxial, power, and specialty cables; and an assortment of sensors and sensor-based technologies. The company distributes its products through a multi-channel approach, utilizing its internal sales force, independent representatives, and an extensive network of electronics distributors. Its diverse customer base comprises original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), electronic manufacturing services (EMS) providers, original design manufacturers (ODMs), and service providers. These clients span numerous industries, including automotive, broadband communication, commercial aerospace, industrial, information technology and data communication, military, mobile device, and mobile network markets. Amphenol Corporation was founded in 1932 and is presently headquartered in Wallingford, Connecticut.",
    "description_en": "Amphenol Corporation, alongside its numerous subsidiaries, operates globally as a prominent designer, manufacturer, and distributor of electrical, electronic, and fiber optic connectors. Its market reach extends across the United States, China, and various international territories. The company is organized into three primary operational divisions: Harsh Environment Solutions, Communications Solutions, and Interconnect and Sensor Systems. Amphenol's comprehensive product lineup features an extensive array of connectors and integrated connector systems. These include specialized interconnects engineered for demanding conditions (covering data, power, high-speed, fiber optic, and radio frequency applications), in addition to busbars and complete power distribution systems. Beyond these core offerings, the company provides value-added products such as backplane interconnect systems, bespoke cable assemblies and harnesses, and cable management solutions. Their portfolio also encompasses flexible and rigid printed circuit boards (PCBs), hinges, and various other mechanical and production-related components. Furthermore, Amphenol supplies antennas for consumer electronics, network infrastructure, and other uses; a range of coaxial, power, and specialty cables; and an assortment of sensors and sensor-based technologies. The company distributes its products through a multi-channel approach, utilizing its internal sales force, independent representatives, and an extensive network of electronics distributors. Its diverse customer base comprises original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), electronic manufacturing services (EMS) providers, original design manufacturers (ODMs), and service providers. These clients span numerous industries, including automotive, broadband communication, commercial aerospace, industrial, information technology and data communication, military, mobile device, and mobile network markets. Amphenol Corporation was founded in 1932 and is presently headquartered in Wallingford, Connecticut.",
    "description_zh": "安費諾公司 (Amphenol Corporation, APH) 為全球領先之電氣、電子、光纖連接器、感測器及其相關互連系統之設計、製造與銷售廠商。其業務範圍遍及全球，涵蓋美國、中國及國際市場。公司營運主要劃分為三大事業部門：惡劣環境解決方案、通訊解決方案，以及互連與感測器系統。\n\n安費諾的核心產品為各類連接器，涵蓋數據、電源、高速、光纖、射頻等應用，並提供整合連接系統、匯流排與完整配電系統。產品組合亦延伸至高附加價值解決方案，如背板互連系統、客製化線束與電纜管理方案。同時供應軟硬式印刷電路板(PCB)、絞鏈及各類機械元件。此外，安費諾提供應用於消費電子與網路基礎設施之天線、同軸/電源/特種電纜，以及多樣化感測器及相關技術。\n\n公司透過內部銷售團隊、獨立代理商及廣泛的電子產品經銷網路進行產品分銷。服務對象廣泛，包括原始設備製造商(OEMs)、電子製造服務(EMS)供應商、原始設計製造商(ODMs)及服務供應商。其終端應用涵蓋汽車、寬頻通訊、商用航空、工業、資訊科技與數據通訊、軍事、行動裝置與行動網路等多元產業。",
