    "description": "Comcast Corporation functions as a global media and technology conglomerate. Its diverse operations are segmented across Cable Communications, Media, Studios, Theme Parks, and Sky. The Cable Communications division delivers internet, television, phone, and mobile services to residential and business clients under its Xfinity brand, alongside offering advertising solutions. Its Media segment encompasses NBCUniversal's television and streaming platforms, including its national, regional, and international cable channels, the NBC and Telemundo broadcast networks, and the Peacock streaming service. The Studios segment is responsible for NBCUniversal's film and television production and distribution activities. Through its Theme Parks division, Comcast manages Universal Studios resorts located in Orlando, Florida; Hollywood, California; Osaka, Japan; and Beijing, China. The Sky segment provides direct-to-consumer services such as video, internet, voice, and mobile phone offerings, while its content arm includes entertainment networks, the Sky News channel, and Sky Sports networks. Additionally, Comcast owns the Philadelphia Flyers hockey team and the Wells Fargo Center arena in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1963, Comcast Corporation is headquartered in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.",
    "description_en": "Comcast Corporation functions as a global media and technology conglomerate. Its diverse operations are segmented across Cable Communications, Media, Studios, Theme Parks, and Sky. The Cable Communications division delivers internet, television, phone, and mobile services to residential and business clients under its Xfinity brand, alongside offering advertising solutions. Its Media segment encompasses NBCUniversal's television and streaming platforms, including its national, regional, and international cable channels, the NBC and Telemundo broadcast networks, and the Peacock streaming service. The Studios segment is responsible for NBCUniversal's film and television production and distribution activities. Through its Theme Parks division, Comcast manages Universal Studios resorts located in Orlando, Florida; Hollywood, California; Osaka, Japan; and Beijing, China. The Sky segment provides direct-to-consumer services such as video, internet, voice, and mobile phone offerings, while its content arm includes entertainment networks, the Sky News channel, and Sky Sports networks. Additionally, Comcast owns the Philadelphia Flyers hockey team and the Wells Fargo Center arena in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1963, Comcast Corporation is headquartered in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.",
    "description_zh": "Comcast Corporation (CMCSA) 作為一家全球性的媒體科技集團，其核心業務橫跨多個板塊：\n\n「有線通訊」(Cable Communications) 部門透過 Xfinity 品牌，為住宅及企業客戶提供寬頻上網、有線電視、語音及行動通訊服務，並提供廣告解決方案。此為其基礎設施與技術驅動的核心服務。\n\n「媒體」(Media) 板塊涵蓋 NBC 環球旗下的電視及串流媒體平台，包括全國性、地方性與國際性有線頻道，以及 NBC 和 Telemundo 廣播網路，並經營 Peacock 串流服務，展現其內容製作與數位發行能力。\n\n「影業」(Studios) 板塊負責 NBC 環球的影視內容製作與全球發行。\n\n「主題樂園」(Theme Parks) 部門則經營位於美國奧蘭多、好萊塢，以及日本大阪、中國北京的環球影城度假村，是其體驗式娛樂業務。\n\n「天空廣播」(Sky) 部門提供影音、寬頻、語音及行動通訊等 DTC（直接面向消費者）服務，其內容業務包含娛樂頻道、Sky News 新聞台及 Sky Sports 體育頻道。\n\n公司總部位於賓州費城。",
