    "description": "NIKE, Inc., through its various subsidiaries, operates as a global enterprise focused on the design, development, marketing, and sale of athletic footwear, apparel, equipment, and accessories for all ages and genders. Beyond its primary offerings, the company provides a range of athletic and casual footwear, clothing, and accessories under the notable Jumpman trademark. It also distributes a variety of casual sneakers, apparel, and accessories, featuring well-known brands like Converse, Chuck Taylor, All Star, One Star, Star Chevron, and Jack Purcell. Under the NIKE brand itself, the company supplies a comprehensive line of performance sports gear and accessories, such as bags, socks, sports balls, eyewear, timepieces, digital devices, bats, gloves, and protective equipment. Additionally, NIKE sells various plastic products to other manufacturers. The company also markets sportswear adorned with licensed logos from college and professional sports teams and leagues. Furthermore, it engages in licensing arrangements, allowing unaffiliated parties to manufacture and sell apparel, digital devices, applications, and other sports equipment under NIKE-owned trademarks. Its extensive product catalog reaches consumers globally through diverse channels, including specialized footwear, sporting goods, athletic specialty, department, skate, tennis, and golf stores. Distribution occurs via NIKE's proprietary retail outlets, digital e-commerce platforms, independent distributors, authorized licensees, and sales representatives. Founded in 1964, the company was originally named Blue Ribbon Sports, Inc., before officially becoming NIKE, Inc. in 1971, and maintains its corporate headquarters in Beaverton, Oregon.",
    "description_en": "NIKE, Inc., through its various subsidiaries, operates as a global enterprise focused on the design, development, marketing, and sale of athletic footwear, apparel, equipment, and accessories for all ages and genders. Beyond its primary offerings, the company provides a range of athletic and casual footwear, clothing, and accessories under the notable Jumpman trademark. It also distributes a variety of casual sneakers, apparel, and accessories, featuring well-known brands like Converse, Chuck Taylor, All Star, One Star, Star Chevron, and Jack Purcell. Under the NIKE brand itself, the company supplies a comprehensive line of performance sports gear and accessories, such as bags, socks, sports balls, eyewear, timepieces, digital devices, bats, gloves, and protective equipment. Additionally, NIKE sells various plastic products to other manufacturers. The company also markets sportswear adorned with licensed logos from college and professional sports teams and leagues. Furthermore, it engages in licensing arrangements, allowing unaffiliated parties to manufacture and sell apparel, digital devices, applications, and other sports equipment under NIKE-owned trademarks. Its extensive product catalog reaches consumers globally through diverse channels, including specialized footwear, sporting goods, athletic specialty, department, skate, tennis, and golf stores. Distribution occurs via NIKE's proprietary retail outlets, digital e-commerce platforms, independent distributors, authorized licensees, and sales representatives. Founded in 1964, the company was originally named Blue Ribbon Sports, Inc., before officially becoming NIKE, Inc. in 1971, and maintains its corporate headquarters in Beaverton, Oregon.",
    "description_zh": "NIKE, Inc.（紐約證券交易所代碼：NKE）作為一家全球領先的運動用品公司，主要從事運動鞋、服飾、裝備及配件之設計、研發、行銷與銷售，服務各年齡層與性別。\n\n其旗下品牌組合多元，涵蓋 **Jordan（Jumpman 商標）**，提供運動與休閒鞋款、服飾及配件；以及 **Converse**（包含 Chuck Taylor、All Star 等經典系列）的休閒鞋履、服飾與配件。NIKE 品牌自身則涵蓋多元高性能運動裝備與配件，如包款、襪類、球類、眼鏡、計時器、數位裝置、球棒、手套及防護器材等。\n\n此外，NIKE亦供應塑膠製品予其他製造商，並行銷授權大學與職業運動隊伍標誌之運動服飾。公司同時透過授權模式，允許第三方夥伴製造與銷售使用其旗下商標之服飾、數位應用及運動器材。\n\n其產品透過全球多元通路觸達消費者，包含專業鞋類店、運動用品店、百貨公司、NIKE自有零售據點、官方數位電商平台、獨立經銷商及授權代理商等。公司創立於1964年，總部位於美國奧勒岡州比弗頓。",
