    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/F.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/F.png",
    "website": "https://www.ford.com",
    "ceo": "James Duncan Farley Jr.",
    "full_time_employees": "169000",
    "description": "Ford Motor Company is a global automotive giant, engaged in the design, production, and servicing of a broad spectrum of vehicles. Its product line encompasses Ford trucks, commercial cars and vans, and sport utility vehicles, in addition to luxury models from its Lincoln brand. The company structures its diverse operations into distinct segments: Ford Blue, Ford Model e, Ford Pro, Ford Next, and Ford Credit. Ford distributes its vehicles, service components, and accessories through a worldwide network of distributors and dealerships. It also supplies directly to large organizational clients, including commercial fleet operators, daily rental companies, and government entities, often facilitated by its established dealerships. Beyond manufacturing and sales, Ford provides substantial financial services. This includes offering retail installment contracts for both new and used vehicles, as well as direct financing leases for new vehicles to a wide range of customers – from individual consumers to commercial enterprises such as leasing companies, government agencies, and fleet providers. Furthermore, the company extends wholesale loans to dealers to facilitate inventory purchases. It also offers capital to dealers for operational expenses, facility enhancements, real estate acquisitions, and other business initiatives. Founded in 1903, Ford Motor Company is headquartered in Dearborn, Michigan.",
    "description_en": "Ford Motor Company is a global automotive giant, engaged in the design, production, and servicing of a broad spectrum of vehicles. Its product line encompasses Ford trucks, commercial cars and vans, and sport utility vehicles, in addition to luxury models from its Lincoln brand. The company structures its diverse operations into distinct segments: Ford Blue, Ford Model e, Ford Pro, Ford Next, and Ford Credit. Ford distributes its vehicles, service components, and accessories through a worldwide network of distributors and dealerships. It also supplies directly to large organizational clients, including commercial fleet operators, daily rental companies, and government entities, often facilitated by its established dealerships. Beyond manufacturing and sales, Ford provides substantial financial services. This includes offering retail installment contracts for both new and used vehicles, as well as direct financing leases for new vehicles to a wide range of customers – from individual consumers to commercial enterprises such as leasing companies, government agencies, and fleet providers. Furthermore, the company extends wholesale loans to dealers to facilitate inventory purchases. It also offers capital to dealers for operational expenses, facility enhancements, real estate acquisitions, and other business initiatives. Founded in 1903, Ford Motor Company is headquartered in Dearborn, Michigan.",
    "description_zh": "福特汽車公司 (F) 為全球領先之汽車製造商，專精於各類車輛之設計、製造與售後服務。其業務範疇涵蓋福特品牌之卡車、商用車、廂型車及運動休旅車 (SUV)，並包含豪華車品牌Lincoln。公司業務營運劃分為Ford Blue、Ford Model e、Ford Pro、Ford Next與Ford Credit等五大板塊。福特透過全球經銷商網絡，銷售旗下各品牌車輛、零件與售後服務配件；亦直接供貨予企業客戶，如商用車隊營運商、汽車租賃公司及政府機關，多透過經銷商通路完成。\n\n除整車產銷外，福特亦提供多元金融服務。服務範疇涵蓋新舊車零售分期合約、新車直接租賃融資，客戶遍及個人、租賃業者、政府機構及車隊服務供應商等商業實體。同時，提供經銷商批發性貸款以購置庫存，並提供營運週轉、設施改善、不動產取得及其他業務拓展所需資金。福特汽車於1903年創立，總部設於密西根州迪爾伯恩。",
