    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/BAC.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/BAC.png",
    "website": "https://www.bankofamerica.com",
    "ceo": "Brian T. Moynihan",
    "full_time_employees": "209911",
    "description": "Operating globally through its various subsidiaries, Bank of America Corporation offers a comprehensive range of banking and financial products and services. Its extensive clientele includes individual consumers, small and mid-market businesses, institutional investors, large corporations, and government bodies worldwide. The Consumer Banking division provides diverse options such as traditional and money market savings accounts, certificates of deposit, individual retirement accounts (IRAs), and both interest-bearing and non-interest-bearing checking accounts, in addition to investment products. This segment also issues credit and debit cards, originates residential mortgages and home equity loans, and offers direct and indirect financing for needs like automotive purchases, recreational vehicles, and personal loans. Within its Global Wealth & Investment Management segment, the company delivers investment management, brokerage, banking, and trust and retirement solutions. It also crafts tailored wealth management strategies, including specialized asset management services. The Global Banking segment furnishes a broad spectrum of lending products, including commercial loans, leases, commitment facilities, trade finance, and both commercial real estate and asset-based lending. Furthermore, it provides treasury solutions such as cash management, foreign exchange, short-term investment options, and merchant services, alongside working capital management guidance. This segment also engages in debt and equity underwriting, distribution, and advisory services related to mergers and acquisitions. Through its Global Markets segment, Bank of America performs market-making activities, offers financing, and provides securities clearing, settlement, and custody services. It also devises risk management products employing interest rate, equity, credit, currency, and commodity derivatives, as well as foreign exchange, fixed-income, and mortgage-related instruments. As of December 31, 2021, the corporation served approximately 67 million consumer and small business clients. Its widespread infrastructure comprised around 4,200 retail financial centers and approximately 16,000 ATMs, supplemented by digital banking platforms utilized by roughly 41 million active users. Founded in 1784, Bank of America is headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina.",
    "description_en": "Operating globally through its various subsidiaries, Bank of America Corporation offers a comprehensive range of banking and financial products and services. Its extensive clientele includes individual consumers, small and mid-market businesses, institutional investors, large corporations, and government bodies worldwide. The Consumer Banking division provides diverse options such as traditional and money market savings accounts, certificates of deposit, individual retirement accounts (IRAs), and both interest-bearing and non-interest-bearing checking accounts, in addition to investment products. This segment also issues credit and debit cards, originates residential mortgages and home equity loans, and offers direct and indirect financing for needs like automotive purchases, recreational vehicles, and personal loans. Within its Global Wealth & Investment Management segment, the company delivers investment management, brokerage, banking, and trust and retirement solutions. It also crafts tailored wealth management strategies, including specialized asset management services. The Global Banking segment furnishes a broad spectrum of lending products, including commercial loans, leases, commitment facilities, trade finance, and both commercial real estate and asset-based lending. Furthermore, it provides treasury solutions such as cash management, foreign exchange, short-term investment options, and merchant services, alongside working capital management guidance. This segment also engages in debt and equity underwriting, distribution, and advisory services related to mergers and acquisitions. Through its Global Markets segment, Bank of America performs market-making activities, offers financing, and provides securities clearing, settlement, and custody services. It also devises risk management products employing interest rate, equity, credit, currency, and commodity derivatives, as well as foreign exchange, fixed-income, and mortgage-related instruments. As of December 31, 2021, the corporation served approximately 67 million consumer and small business clients. Its widespread infrastructure comprised around 4,200 retail financial centers and approximately 16,000 ATMs, supplemented by digital banking platforms utilized by roughly 41 million active users. Founded in 1784, Bank of America is headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina.",
    "description_zh": "美國銀行 (Bank of America Corporation, BAC) 作為全球領先的金融服務集團，透過旗下子公司，提供廣泛的銀行及金融產品與服務。其客戶群涵蓋個人消費者、中小企業、機構投資人、大型企業及政府實體。\n\n**消費金融部門** 提供多元存款帳戶（如儲蓄、貨幣市場帳戶、定期存款）、個人退休帳戶(IRA)、支票帳戶，並搭配投資商品。同時發行信用卡與簽帳卡，承作住宅房貸、房屋淨值信用額度，並為汽車、休閒車及個人需求提供直接與間接融資方案。\n\n**全球財富暨投資管理部門** 則提供投資管理、證券經紀業務、銀行服務、信託及退休金解決方案，並為客戶規劃客製化財富管理策略，包含專業資產管理服務。\n\n**全球銀行部門** 提供多元授信產品，如商業貸款、租賃、循環信貸額度、貿易融資、商業不動產及資產擔保貸款。此外，亦提供財資管理方案，包括現金管理、外匯、短期投資、商家收單服務，以及營運資金管理諮詢。本部門亦參與債券與股票的承銷、銷售與併購諮詢服務。\n\n**全球市場部門** 從事市場造市、提供融資，並提供證券清算、交割與保管服務。同時，其開發利率、股票、信用、貨幣、商品等衍生性金融商品，以及外匯、固定收益與房貸相關工具，以協助客戶管理風險。\n\n截至2021年底，美國銀行服務約6,700萬個人及中小企業客戶，擁有約4,200個實體金融服務據點與約16,000台自動櫃員機(ATM)，並透過其**數位銀行平台**服務約4,100萬活躍數位用戶。總部設於北卡羅來納州夏洛特。",
