    "ceo": "David Michael Solomon",
    "full_time_employees": "47400",
    "description": "The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc. (GS) operates as a prominent global financial services firm, offering an extensive array of services to corporations, financial institutions, governmental bodies, and individuals worldwide. The company's operations are organized into four primary divisions: Investment Banking, Global Markets, Asset Management, and Consumer & Wealth Management. The Investment Banking segment furnishes strategic advisory services covering intricate transactions such as mergers, acquisitions, divestitures, corporate defense strategies, restructurings, and spin-offs. It also extends various lending facilities, including middle-market, relationship, and acquisition financing, in addition to transaction banking services. This division further specializes in underwriting, assisting clients with equity offerings for common, preferred, and convertible securities, as well as debt offerings encompassing investment-grade, high-yield, bank/bridge loans, and emerging market debt instruments, alongside the creation of structured securities. Within its Global Markets division, Goldman Sachs engages in client execution activities for both cash and derivative instruments, provides solutions for credit and interest rate products, and offers comprehensive equity intermediation, financing, clearing, settlement, and custody services. This segment also transacts in products linked to mortgages, foreign exchange, commodities, and equities. The Asset Management segment is responsible for managing assets across a diverse spectrum of classes, including equities, fixed income, hedge funds, credit funds, private equity, real estate, currencies, and commodities. It delivers tailored investment advisory solutions and makes direct investments in corporate entities, real estate ventures, and infrastructure projects. The Consumer & Wealth Management segment provides individual clients with wealth advisory and banking services. These include financial planning, investment management, deposit-taking, and lending. It also offers private banking services, unsecured loans, and accepts savings and time deposits. Founded in 1869, the company's corporate headquarters are located in New York, New York.",
    "description_en": "The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc. (GS) operates as a prominent global financial services firm, offering an extensive array of services to corporations, financial institutions, governmental bodies, and individuals worldwide. The company's operations are organized into four primary divisions: Investment Banking, Global Markets, Asset Management, and Consumer & Wealth Management. The Investment Banking segment furnishes strategic advisory services covering intricate transactions such as mergers, acquisitions, divestitures, corporate defense strategies, restructurings, and spin-offs. It also extends various lending facilities, including middle-market, relationship, and acquisition financing, in addition to transaction banking services. This division further specializes in underwriting, assisting clients with equity offerings for common, preferred, and convertible securities, as well as debt offerings encompassing investment-grade, high-yield, bank/bridge loans, and emerging market debt instruments, alongside the creation of structured securities. Within its Global Markets division, Goldman Sachs engages in client execution activities for both cash and derivative instruments, provides solutions for credit and interest rate products, and offers comprehensive equity intermediation, financing, clearing, settlement, and custody services. This segment also transacts in products linked to mortgages, foreign exchange, commodities, and equities. The Asset Management segment is responsible for managing assets across a diverse spectrum of classes, including equities, fixed income, hedge funds, credit funds, private equity, real estate, currencies, and commodities. It delivers tailored investment advisory solutions and makes direct investments in corporate entities, real estate ventures, and infrastructure projects. The Consumer & Wealth Management segment provides individual clients with wealth advisory and banking services. These include financial planning, investment management, deposit-taking, and lending. It also offers private banking services, unsecured loans, and accepts savings and time deposits. Founded in 1869, the company's corporate headquarters are located in New York, New York.",
    "description_zh": "高盛集團（The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc.，GS）是一家全球領先的金融服務機構，為企業、金融機構、政府機關及個人客戶提供全方位的專業服務。其業務劃分為四大主要板塊：投資銀行、全球市場、資產管理，以及消費與財富管理。\n\n投資銀行部門提供企業客戶策略性諮詢服務，涵蓋複雜的併購、資產剝離、企業防禦策略、重整及分拆交易。同時提供中型市場、關係型、併購融資等多樣授信服務及交易銀行解決方案。此外，亦承銷股權與債務發行，包括普通股、特別股、可轉換證券、投資級與高收益債、銀行/過渡性貸款及新興市場債務工具，並參與結構型證券的設計與發行。\n\n全球市場部門為客戶執行現金與衍生性商品交易，提供信用與利率產品解決方案，涵蓋股權中介、融資、清算、交割及保管等服務，並從事抵押貸款、外匯、大宗商品及股權相關商品的交易業務。\n\n資產管理部門負責管理多元資產類別，包括股票、固定收益、對沖基金、信用基金、私募股權、房地產、貨幣及大宗商品。提供客製化投資諮詢方案，並直接投資企業、房地產與基礎建設項目。\n\n消費與財富管理部門則為個人客戶提供財富諮詢與銀行服務，服務內容涵蓋財務規劃、投資管理、存款、貸款、私人銀行服務、無擔保貸款，以及活期與定期存款業務。公司創立於1869年，總部設於紐約州紐約市。",
