    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/AXP.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/AXP.png",
    "website": "https://www.americanexpress.com",
    "ceo": "Stephen Joseph Squeri",
    "full_time_employees": "76800",
    "description": "Operating globally, American Express Company and its affiliated entities deliver a comprehensive suite of charge and credit payment card solutions, alongside a variety of travel-related offerings. Its business structure is organized into three primary divisions: the Global Consumer Services Group, Global Commercial Services, and Global Merchant and Network Services. Among its core offerings are diverse payment and financing instruments, robust network infrastructure services, tools for managing accounts payable expenses, and comprehensive travel and lifestyle support. Furthermore, it facilitates merchant services such as acquisition, transaction processing, settlement, and point-of-sale marketing, providing vital information and assistance to businesses. The company also specializes in fraud mitigation and developing and managing customer loyalty initiatives. These products and services are made available to a broad clientele, encompassing individual consumers, small and mid-sized enterprises, and large corporate entities. Distribution channels include digital platforms (mobile and online applications), collaborations with third-party vendors and partners, direct communication methods like mail and telephone, dedicated internal sales forces, and direct response advertising campaigns. Established in 1850, American Express Company maintains its corporate headquarters in New York, New York.",
    "description_en": "Operating globally, American Express Company and its affiliated entities deliver a comprehensive suite of charge and credit payment card solutions, alongside a variety of travel-related offerings. Its business structure is organized into three primary divisions: the Global Consumer Services Group, Global Commercial Services, and Global Merchant and Network Services. Among its core offerings are diverse payment and financing instruments, robust network infrastructure services, tools for managing accounts payable expenses, and comprehensive travel and lifestyle support. Furthermore, it facilitates merchant services such as acquisition, transaction processing, settlement, and point-of-sale marketing, providing vital information and assistance to businesses. The company also specializes in fraud mitigation and developing and managing customer loyalty initiatives. These products and services are made available to a broad clientele, encompassing individual consumers, small and mid-sized enterprises, and large corporate entities. Distribution channels include digital platforms (mobile and online applications), collaborations with third-party vendors and partners, direct communication methods like mail and telephone, dedicated internal sales forces, and direct response advertising campaigns. Established in 1850, American Express Company maintains its corporate headquarters in New York, New York.",
    "description_zh": "美國運通公司 (American Express Company, AXP) 是一家全球性金融服務企業，其核心業務涵蓋簽帳卡、信用卡支付解決方案，以及多元的旅遊與生活風格服務。公司營運架構分為三大事業體：全球個人消費服務、全球企業客戶服務，以及全球商戶與網路服務。\n\nAXP 提供豐富的支付與融資工具、先進的支付網路基礎設施服務、應付帳款費用管理方案，並提供全方位的旅遊與生活風格支援。此外，公司亦專精於商戶收單、交易處理、清算結算及銷售點行銷，為企業客戶提供關鍵資訊與支援。其服務範圍還包括詐欺風險管理與客戶忠誠計畫的開發與推動。\n\n目標客群廣泛，涵蓋個人消費者、中小型企業 (SMEs) 及大型企業客戶。服務通路多元，包含數位平台（如行動與線上應用程式）、第三方合作夥伴、郵件與電話直效溝通、內部專業銷售團隊，以及直效行銷活動。美國運通總部位於紐約市，自1850年成立至今。",
