    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TRU.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TRU.png",
    "website": "https://www.transunion.com",
    "ceo": "Christopher A. Cartwright",
    "full_time_employees": "13500",
    "description": "TransUnion operates as a global consumer credit reporting agency that provides risk and information solutions. The company operates in two segments, U.S. Markets and International. The U.S. Markets segment provides credit reporting, credit marketing, analytics and consulting, identity verification, and authentication and debt recovery solutions for financial services industry; and onboarding and transaction processing products, scoring and analytic products, marketing solutions, fraud and identity management solutions, and customer retention solutions, as well select market-specific solutions for insurance, technology, retail and e-commerce, telecommunications, media, tenant and employment screening, collections, and public sectors. It also offers credit reports, scores, and freezes credit monitoring, identity protection and resolution, and financial management for consumers, as well as helps businesses respond to data breach events through its own websites, as well as channels. The International segment offers credit reports, analytics, technology solutions, and other value-added risk management services; consumer services, which helps consumers to manage their personal finances; credit bureaus; and consumer and business credit reporting, insurance and auto information solutions, and commercial credit information services. This segment serves customers in financial services, retail credit, insurance, automotive, collections, public sector, and communications industries through direct and indirect channels. The company was formerly known as TransUnion Holding Company, Inc. and changed its name to TransUnion in March 2015. TransUnion was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.",
    "description_en": "TransUnion operates as a global consumer credit reporting agency that provides risk and information solutions. The company operates in two segments, U.S. Markets and International. The U.S. Markets segment provides credit reporting, credit marketing, analytics and consulting, identity verification, and authentication and debt recovery solutions for financial services industry; and onboarding and transaction processing products, scoring and analytic products, marketing solutions, fraud and identity management solutions, and customer retention solutions, as well select market-specific solutions for insurance, technology, retail and e-commerce, telecommunications, media, tenant and employment screening, collections, and public sectors. It also offers credit reports, scores, and freezes credit monitoring, identity protection and resolution, and financial management for consumers, as well as helps businesses respond to data breach events through its own websites, as well as channels. The International segment offers credit reports, analytics, technology solutions, and other value-added risk management services; consumer services, which helps consumers to manage their personal finances; credit bureaus; and consumer and business credit reporting, insurance and auto information solutions, and commercial credit information services. This segment serves customers in financial services, retail credit, insurance, automotive, collections, public sector, and communications industries through direct and indirect channels. The company was formerly known as TransUnion Holding Company, Inc. and changed its name to TransUnion in March 2015. TransUnion was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.",
    "description_zh": "TransUnion (TRU) 是一家全球性消費者信用報告機構，核心業務為提供風險與資訊解決方案。其營運主要劃分為美國市場與國際市場兩大事業體。\n\n美國市場事業體專為金融服務業提供信用報告、信用行銷、數據分析與諮詢、身份驗證及債務催收等解決方案。此外，亦為保險、科技、零售電商、電信媒體、租賃僱用篩選、資產催收與公共部門，提供客戶導入與交易處理、信用評分與分析、行銷策略、詐欺與身份管理、以及客戶關係維護等產品與方案。針對一般消費者，則提供信用報告與分數、信用凍結、信用監測、身份保護與金融管理等服務，並協助企業應對資料外洩事件。\n\n國際市場事業體則提供信用報告、數據分析、技術解決方案及多元加值型風險管理服務，包含協助消費者管理個人財務的服務，並營運多個信用局，提供消費者與企業信用報告、保險與汽車資訊解決方案，以及商業信用資訊服務。其服務客群涵蓋金融、零售信用、保險、汽車、資產催收、公共部門與通訊業。",
