    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CVX.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CVX.png",
    "website": "https://www.chevron.com",
    "ceo": "Michael K. Wirth",
    "full_time_employees": "43039",
    "description": "Chevron Corporation functions as a global energy and chemicals powerhouse, orchestrating its diverse operations worldwide. The company's business is organized into two primary divisions: Upstream and Downstream. The Upstream segment focuses on the full lifecycle of crude oil and natural gas, from their initial exploration and development to production and subsequent transportation. This also encompasses the processing, liquefaction, transit, and regasification of liquefied natural gas (LNG), as well as pipeline transport of crude oil and the movement, storage, and sale of natural gas. Additionally, this segment manages a facility dedicated to converting natural gas into liquid fuels. In contrast, the Downstream segment is tasked with refining crude oil into a variety of petroleum products. Its activities include the merchandising of crude oil, refined goods, and lubricants, in addition to the creation and distribution of renewable fuels. This division is also responsible for moving crude oil and refined products using a range of methods, including pipelines, ships, motor vehicles, and rail cars. Furthermore, it produces and markets bulk petrochemicals, industrial-grade plastics, and additives for both fuels and lubricants. Beyond these core ventures, Chevron is also involved in financial management, debt financing, insurance underwriting, real estate development, and various technology-driven enterprises. Founded in 1879, the company operated as ChevronTexaco Corporation until it officially became Chevron Corporation in 2005. Its corporate headquarters are situated in San Ramon, California.",
    "description_en": "Chevron Corporation functions as a global energy and chemicals powerhouse, orchestrating its diverse operations worldwide. The company's business is organized into two primary divisions: Upstream and Downstream. The Upstream segment focuses on the full lifecycle of crude oil and natural gas, from their initial exploration and development to production and subsequent transportation. This also encompasses the processing, liquefaction, transit, and regasification of liquefied natural gas (LNG), as well as pipeline transport of crude oil and the movement, storage, and sale of natural gas. Additionally, this segment manages a facility dedicated to converting natural gas into liquid fuels. In contrast, the Downstream segment is tasked with refining crude oil into a variety of petroleum products. Its activities include the merchandising of crude oil, refined goods, and lubricants, in addition to the creation and distribution of renewable fuels. This division is also responsible for moving crude oil and refined products using a range of methods, including pipelines, ships, motor vehicles, and rail cars. Furthermore, it produces and markets bulk petrochemicals, industrial-grade plastics, and additives for both fuels and lubricants. Beyond these core ventures, Chevron is also involved in financial management, debt financing, insurance underwriting, real estate development, and various technology-driven enterprises. Founded in 1879, the company operated as ChevronTexaco Corporation until it officially became Chevron Corporation in 2005. Its corporate headquarters are situated in San Ramon, California.",
    "description_zh": "雪佛龍公司 (Chevron Corporation, CVX) 是一家全球性的綜合能源及石化巨擘，業務營運遍及全球。其核心事業體分為兩大板塊：「上游事業」與「下游事業」。\n\n「上游事業」涵蓋原油與天然氣的完整生命週期，從探勘、開發、生產到運輸。此範疇亦包括液化天然氣 (LNG) 的處理、液化、轉運、再氣化，原油的管線運輸，以及天然氣的轉運、儲存與銷售。此外，上游事業也管理將天然氣轉化為液體燃料 (Gas-to-liquids, GTL) 的生產設施。\n\n「下游事業」則負責將原油精煉成各式石油產品，並從事原油、精煉產品與潤滑油的貿易與銷售，以及再生燃料的生產與配送。此事業體透過管線、船隻、汽車及鐵路等多元方式，運輸原油及精煉產品。同時，也生產與銷售大宗石化產品、工業級塑膠，以及燃料與潤滑油添加劑。\n\n除核心業務外，雪佛龍亦涉足財務管理、債務融資、保險承銷、不動產開發及各類科技相關企業。公司創立於1879年，總部設於加州聖拉蒙。",
