    "ceo": "Gregory L. Ebel",
    "full_time_employees": "14800",
    "description": "Enbridge Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an energy infrastructure company. The company operates through four segments: Liquids Pipelines, Gas Transmission, Gas Distribution and Storage, and Renewable Power Generation. The Liquids Pipelines segment operates pipelines and related terminals to transport, store, and export various grades of crude oil and other liquid hydrocarbons in Canada and the United States. This segment also provides physical commodity marketing and logistical services, and crude oil marketing services. The Gas Transmission segment invests in natural gas pipelines and gathering and processing facilities in Canada and the United States. The Gas Distribution and Storage segment is involved in natural gas utility operations serving residential, commercial, and industrial customers in Ontario, as well as natural gas distribution activities in Quebec. The Renewable Power Generation segment operates wind, solar, geothermal, waste heat recovery, and transmission assets in North America. The company was formerly known as IPL Energy Inc. and changed its name to Enbridge Inc. in October 1998. Enbridge Inc. was founded in 1949 and is headquartered in Calgary, Canada.",
    "description_en": "Enbridge Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an energy infrastructure company. The company operates through four segments: Liquids Pipelines, Gas Transmission, Gas Distribution and Storage, and Renewable Power Generation. The Liquids Pipelines segment operates pipelines and related terminals to transport, store, and export various grades of crude oil and other liquid hydrocarbons in Canada and the United States. This segment also provides physical commodity marketing and logistical services, and crude oil marketing services. The Gas Transmission segment invests in natural gas pipelines and gathering and processing facilities in Canada and the United States. The Gas Distribution and Storage segment is involved in natural gas utility operations serving residential, commercial, and industrial customers in Ontario, as well as natural gas distribution activities in Quebec. The Renewable Power Generation segment operates wind, solar, geothermal, waste heat recovery, and transmission assets in North America. The company was formerly known as IPL Energy Inc. and changed its name to Enbridge Inc. in October 1998. Enbridge Inc. was founded in 1949 and is headquartered in Calgary, Canada.",
    "description_zh": "安橋公司 (Enbridge Inc.) 為北美領先的能源基礎設施企業，主要營運範疇涵蓋四大事業部。其中，**液態碳氫化合物管線 (Liquids Pipelines)** 業務於加拿大及美國經營原油與其他液態碳氫化合物之管線、儲存設施及出口業務，並提供實體商品行銷與物流服務；**天然氣傳輸 (Gas Transmission)** 事業則在加、美兩地投資並營運天然氣管線、集輸與處理設施；**天然氣配銷與儲存 (Gas Distribution and Storage)** 業務主要於安大略省為住宅、商業及工業客戶提供天然氣公用事業服務，並在魁北克省進行天然氣配銷；而**再生能源發電 (Renewable Power Generation)** 事業則於北美地區營運風力、太陽能、地熱、餘熱回收發電及輸電資產。",
