    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/KMI.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/KMI.png",
    "website": "https://www.kindermorgan.com",
    "ceo": "Kimberly Allen Dang",
    "full_time_employees": "11028",
    "description": "Kinder Morgan, Inc. operates as a leading energy infrastructure company across North America. Its extensive operations are categorized into four primary business segments: Natural Gas Pipelines, Products Pipelines, Terminals, and CO2. The Natural Gas Pipelines segment manages a vast network of interstate and intrastate natural gas pipelines, along with underground storage systems. This includes natural gas gathering systems, processing and treatment facilities, natural gas liquids fractionation plants, transportation systems, and infrastructure for liquefied natural gas liquefaction and storage. Within its Products Pipelines segment, the company owns and operates pipelines designed for refined petroleum products, crude oil, and condensate, supported by associated product terminals and facilities for petroleum pipeline transmix. The Terminals segment involves the ownership and operation of both liquid and bulk terminals that are utilized for storing and handling a wide array of commodities, such as gasoline, diesel fuel, various chemicals, ethanol, metals, and petroleum coke. This division also includes the ownership of tankers. Lastly, the CO2 segment is dedicated to the production, transportation, and marketing of carbon dioxide, primarily for enhanced oil recovery from mature oil fields. This segment also holds interests in or operates oil fields and gasoline processing plants, oversees a crude oil pipeline system located in West Texas, and manages renewable natural gas (RNG) and liquefied natural gas (LNG) facilities. In total, Kinder Morgan owns and operates approximately 83,000 miles of pipelines and 143 terminals. The company, initially named Kinder Morgan Holdco LLC, officially changed its name to Kinder Morgan, Inc. in February 2011. Founded in 1936, its corporate headquarters are situated in Houston, Texas.",
    "description_en": "Kinder Morgan, Inc. operates as a leading energy infrastructure company across North America. Its extensive operations are categorized into four primary business segments: Natural Gas Pipelines, Products Pipelines, Terminals, and CO2. The Natural Gas Pipelines segment manages a vast network of interstate and intrastate natural gas pipelines, along with underground storage systems. This includes natural gas gathering systems, processing and treatment facilities, natural gas liquids fractionation plants, transportation systems, and infrastructure for liquefied natural gas liquefaction and storage. Within its Products Pipelines segment, the company owns and operates pipelines designed for refined petroleum products, crude oil, and condensate, supported by associated product terminals and facilities for petroleum pipeline transmix. The Terminals segment involves the ownership and operation of both liquid and bulk terminals that are utilized for storing and handling a wide array of commodities, such as gasoline, diesel fuel, various chemicals, ethanol, metals, and petroleum coke. This division also includes the ownership of tankers. Lastly, the CO2 segment is dedicated to the production, transportation, and marketing of carbon dioxide, primarily for enhanced oil recovery from mature oil fields. This segment also holds interests in or operates oil fields and gasoline processing plants, oversees a crude oil pipeline system located in West Texas, and manages renewable natural gas (RNG) and liquefied natural gas (LNG) facilities. In total, Kinder Morgan owns and operates approximately 83,000 miles of pipelines and 143 terminals. The company, initially named Kinder Morgan Holdco LLC, officially changed its name to Kinder Morgan, Inc. in February 2011. Founded in 1936, its corporate headquarters are situated in Houston, Texas.",
    "description_zh": "**美國金德摩根公司（Kinder Morgan, Inc., KMI）**為北美領先的能源基礎設施營運商，業務涵蓋能源價值鏈多個環節。其核心業務共分四大板塊：\n\n1.  **天然氣管線：** 經營廣泛的跨州與州內天然氣管線網路及地下儲存系統，並涵蓋天然氣集輸、處理、分餾廠，以及液化天然氣（LNG）液化與儲存設施。\n2.  **油品管線：** 擁有並營運精煉石油產品、原油、凝析油等運送管線，輔以相關儲運碼頭與油品混合設施。\n3.  **儲運碼頭：** 營運液體與散裝物資終端站，提供汽油、柴油、化學品、乙醇、金屬、石油焦等多種大宗商品之儲存與處理服務，亦擁有油輪。\n4.  **二氧化碳（CO2）：** 主要負責CO2的生產、運輸與銷售，用於成熟油田之強化採油（EOR）。此板塊亦持有或經營油田、汽油處理廠、西德州原油管線系統，並管理再生天然氣（RNG）與LNG設施。\n\nKMI目前總計擁有並營運約8.3萬英里管線及143個儲運站。",
