    "image": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/HAL.png",
    "logo": "https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/HAL.png",
    "website": "https://www.halliburton.com",
    "ceo": "Jeffrey Allen Miller",
    "full_time_employees": "46000",
    "description": "Halliburton Company (HAL) is a global supplier of products and services tailored for the energy sector. Its operations are structured into two primary divisions: Completion and Production, and Drilling and Evaluation. The Completion and Production segment focuses on enhancing well output through techniques like stimulation and sand control. It provides cementing services for well integrity, including casing and bonding, alongside a range of specialized downhole completion tools such as intelligent well systems, liner hangers, and multilateral solutions. This segment also supports production with offerings like coiled tubing, hydraulic workover units, pumping, and nitrogen services, in addition to managing pipeline and process services from initial setup (pre-commissioning, commissioning) through ongoing maintenance and eventual retirement (decommissioning). Furthermore, it supplies electrical submersible pumps and delivers artificial lift solutions. The Drilling and Evaluation segment offers a comprehensive suite of drilling fluids, including systems, performance additives, completion fluids, solids control, specialized testing equipment, and waste management services. It also provides chemicals and associated services for oilfield completion, production, and downstream water and process treatment. This division includes advanced drilling systems, wireline and perforating services encompassing open-hole logging and cased-hole slickline operations, and a variety of drill bits (e.g., roller cone, fixed cutter), hole enlargement tools, and coring services. Moreover, it leverages cloud-based digital services and artificial intelligence on an open architecture to deliver subsurface insights, streamline well construction, and optimize reservoir and production management. Specialized testing and subsea services are also offered for reservoir information analysis and optimization strategies, alongside project management and integrated asset management services. Founded in 1919, Halliburton Company maintains its headquarters in Houston, Texas.",
    "description_en": "Halliburton Company (HAL) is a global supplier of products and services tailored for the energy sector. Its operations are structured into two primary divisions: Completion and Production, and Drilling and Evaluation. The Completion and Production segment focuses on enhancing well output through techniques like stimulation and sand control. It provides cementing services for well integrity, including casing and bonding, alongside a range of specialized downhole completion tools such as intelligent well systems, liner hangers, and multilateral solutions. This segment also supports production with offerings like coiled tubing, hydraulic workover units, pumping, and nitrogen services, in addition to managing pipeline and process services from initial setup (pre-commissioning, commissioning) through ongoing maintenance and eventual retirement (decommissioning). Furthermore, it supplies electrical submersible pumps and delivers artificial lift solutions. The Drilling and Evaluation segment offers a comprehensive suite of drilling fluids, including systems, performance additives, completion fluids, solids control, specialized testing equipment, and waste management services. It also provides chemicals and associated services for oilfield completion, production, and downstream water and process treatment. This division includes advanced drilling systems, wireline and perforating services encompassing open-hole logging and cased-hole slickline operations, and a variety of drill bits (e.g., roller cone, fixed cutter), hole enlargement tools, and coring services. Moreover, it leverages cloud-based digital services and artificial intelligence on an open architecture to deliver subsurface insights, streamline well construction, and optimize reservoir and production management. Specialized testing and subsea services are also offered for reservoir information analysis and optimization strategies, alongside project management and integrated asset management services. Founded in 1919, Halliburton Company maintains its headquarters in Houston, Texas.",
    "description_zh": "荷蘭頓 (Halliburton Company, HAL) 為全球能源產業提供全方位產品與服務，核心業務涵蓋兩大事業部：\n\n1.  **完井與生產 (Completion and Production)**：專注提升油井產能，提供增產、防砂、固井服務，以及智慧油井系統、尾管懸掛器等井下完井工具。亦支援連續油管、液壓修井、泵送與氮氣服務；負責管線製程管理（從建置至退役），並供應電動潛水泵及人工舉升解決方案。\n\n2.  **鑽井與評估 (Drilling and Evaluation)**：提供各式鑽井液、完井液、固體控制、廢棄物管理；油田完井與生產化學品；先進鑽井系統、電纜測井與射孔（含裸眼/套管井）、鑽頭、擴孔工具、取芯等服務。該部門運用開放架構的雲端數位服務及人工智慧 (AI)，提供地下儲層洞察，優化油井建造與油藏管理。亦提供專業測試、水下服務與整合資產管理。",
