    "description": "Southern Copper Corporation engages in mining, exploring, smelting, and refining copper and other minerals in Mexico, the United States, Peru, Brazil, Chile, and Other American countries. The company is involved in the mining, milling, and flotation of copper ore to produce copper and molybdenum concentrates; smelting of copper concentrates to produce blister and anode copper; refining of anode copper to produce copper cathodes; production of copper-molybdenum concentrates and sulfuric acid; production of refined silver, gold, and other materials; and mining and processing of copper, molybdenum, zinc, silver, gold and lead. It operates the Toquepala and Cuajone open-pit mines, smelter, and refinery in Peru; La Caridad, an open-pit copper mine, as well as copper ore concentrator; and SX-EW plant, a smelter, refinery, and rod plant in Mexico. The company also operates Buenavista, an open-pit copper mine, as well as copper concentrators and operating SX-EW plants in Mexico. In addition, it operates underground mines that produce zinc, lead, copper, silver, and gold; coal mine; and zinc refinery. The company has interests in 164,805 hectares and 505,788 hectares of concessions in Peru and Mexico; and 98,634 hectares and 28,453 hectares of exploration concessions in Argentina and Chile. Southern Copper Corporation was formerly known as Southern Peru Copper Corp. and changed its name to Southern Copper Corporation in July 1996. The company was incorporated in 1952 and is based in Phoenix, Arizona. Southern Copper Corporation operates as a subsidiary of Americas Mining Corporation.",
    "description_en": "Southern Copper Corporation engages in mining, exploring, smelting, and refining copper and other minerals in Mexico, the United States, Peru, Brazil, Chile, and Other American countries. The company is involved in the mining, milling, and flotation of copper ore to produce copper and molybdenum concentrates; smelting of copper concentrates to produce blister and anode copper; refining of anode copper to produce copper cathodes; production of copper-molybdenum concentrates and sulfuric acid; production of refined silver, gold, and other materials; and mining and processing of copper, molybdenum, zinc, silver, gold and lead. It operates the Toquepala and Cuajone open-pit mines, smelter, and refinery in Peru; La Caridad, an open-pit copper mine, as well as copper ore concentrator; and SX-EW plant, a smelter, refinery, and rod plant in Mexico. The company also operates Buenavista, an open-pit copper mine, as well as copper concentrators and operating SX-EW plants in Mexico. In addition, it operates underground mines that produce zinc, lead, copper, silver, and gold; coal mine; and zinc refinery. The company has interests in 164,805 hectares and 505,788 hectares of concessions in Peru and Mexico; and 98,634 hectares and 28,453 hectares of exploration concessions in Argentina and Chile. Southern Copper Corporation was formerly known as Southern Peru Copper Corp. and changed its name to Southern Copper Corporation in July 1996. The company was incorporated in 1952 and is based in Phoenix, Arizona. Southern Copper Corporation operates as a subsidiary of Americas Mining Corporation.",
    "description_zh": "**南方銅業公司 (Southern Copper Corporation, SCCO)** 是一家整合性的礦業公司，主要從事銅及其伴生礦之探勘、開採、選礦、冶煉與精煉業務。營運範圍涵蓋墨西哥、秘魯、美國等地，並於秘魯、墨西哥、阿根廷及智利持有總計約80萬公頃的礦區特許權。\n\n核心產品為銅（包含銅精礦、電解銅、陽極銅、粗銅等）、鉬、鋅、銀、金、鉛及硫酸。其業務模式涵蓋完整的供應鏈，從露天及地下礦山開採，經選礦浮選產出銅精礦，繼而進行冶煉生產粗銅、陽極銅，最終透過電解精煉製成高純度電解銅。公司亦運用溶劑萃取電積 (SX-EW) 技術生產銅。\n\n主要礦區與冶煉設施包括秘魯的Toquepala及Cuajone露天礦、冶煉廠與精煉廠；墨西哥的La Caridad及Buenavista露天銅礦、選礦廠、SX-EW廠、冶煉廠、精煉廠及銅桿廠等。此外，公司亦經營生產鋅、鉛、銅、銀、金的地下礦、煤礦及鋅精煉廠。",
